. Actually CD endpoints are (-r1,0) and (d+r2,0). Midpoint is ((-r1 + d + r2)/2, 0). Perpendicular bisector is vertical line x = that value.\n\nNow perpendicular bisector of AC: A = (x, y), C = (-r1,0). Midpoint is ((x - r1)/2, y/2). Slope of AC is (y - 0)/(x + r1) = y/(x + r1). So perpendicular slope is -(x + r1)/y. So equation: (X - (x - r1)/2) = -(x + r1)/y * (Y - y/2). Intersection with vertical line x = (d + r2 - r1)/2 yields P's coordinates. Let's denote X0 = (d + r2 - r1)/2. Then we can solve for Y coordinate: X0 - (x - r1)/2 = -(x + r1)/y * (Y - y/2). So Y = y/2 - (y/(x + r1)) * (X0 - (x - r1)/2). So P = (X0, Y). So P's x-coordinate is fixed as above.\n\nNow MP line: M = (0,0) to P = (X0, Y). So slope = Y/X0.\n\nNow BD line: B = (x, -y), D = (d+r2,0). Slope = (0 + y)/(d+r2 - x) = y/(d+r2 - x). So slope of BD is y/(d+r2 - x). For MP to be parallel to BD, we need Y/X0 = y/(d+r2 - x). Let's compute Y. Y = y/2 - (y/(x + r1)) * (X0 - (x - r1)/2). Compute X0 - (x - r1)/2 = (d + r2 - r1)/2 - (x - r1)/2 = (d + r2 - r1 - x + r1)/2 = (d + r2 - x)/2. So Y = y/2 - (y/(x + r1)) * ((d + r2 - x)/2) = y/2 - (y (d + r2 - x)) / (2 (x + r1)). So Y = y/2 * [1 - (d + r2 - x)/(x + r1)] = y/2 * [(x + r1 - (d + r2 - x)) / (x + r1)] = y/2 * [(x + r1 - d - r2 + x) / (x + r1)] = y/2 * [(2x + r1 - d - r2) / (x + r1)].\n\nThus Y = y * (2x + r1 - d - r2) / (2 (x + r1)). So MP slope = Y / X0 = [y * (2x + r1 - d - r2) / (2 (x + r1))] / [(d + r2 - r1)/2] = y * (2x + r1 - d - r2) / (2 (x + r1)) * 2 / (d + r2 - r1) = y * (2x + r1 - d - r2) / ((x + r1) (d + r2 - r1)). So MP slope = y * (2x + r1 - d - r2) / ((x + r1) (d + r2 - r1)). Meanwhile BD slope = y / (d + r2 - x). So we need equality:\n\ny * (2x + r1 - d - r2) / ((x + r1) (d + r2 - r1)) = y / (d + r2 - x).\n\nCancel y (nonzero unless y=0 which would be degenerate). So\n\n(2x + r1 - d - r2) / ((x + r1) (d + r2 - r1)) = 1 / (d + r2 - x).\n\nCross-multiply:\n\n(2x + r1 - d - r2) * (d + r2 - x) = (x + r1) (d + r2 - r1).\n\nExpand LHS: (2x + 